A. PROBLEM STATEMENT

Design Low-Level Design for Restaurant Reservation System (like Table Booking).

Requirements:

Users can search restaurants by location, cuisine, or rating.
Users can view available tables and time slots.
Users can make, modify, or cancel reservations.
Restaurant admins can manage tables, menus, and availability.
Handle concurrency (multiple users booking the same table at the same time).
Support waitlist if tables are full.

Constraints:

In-memory implementation is acceptable.
Focus on core reservation flow.

Edge Cases:

Table already booked at the same time slot.
Reservation cancellation with refund policy.
No available tables.
Overbooking prevention.

B. HAPPY PATH STORY

=> Rahul wants to book a table for 4 people at "Meghana Foods" for tonight at 8 PM.
